Z||000000||fropuff||11-08-2000||07:37 PM||||Hey, I've been thinking that I want to get more power out of my 2.8 GT.  I was thinking of a supercharger, but that's too expensive.  I want to save my money up for a Northstar.  I was considering a nitrous system.  I know, I've heard bad things about NOS.  I wouldn't use it all the time, just when racing, not much at all.  I was wondering if this would cause premature wear on my engine.  Again, I wouldn't use it much at all, just on certain times I feel a little slow.  I was also wondering where to put a NOS bottle.  I'm pretty sure in the trunk, in the deepest part.  I could then cover that deeper part with a piece of carpeted plywood, then the cops won't know anything about it.  Sorry for getting so long, I just would like to know.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000001||sluppy123||11-08-2000||08:54 PM||||I've got a 70 shot of NOS on my 87' GT with a 2.8 Jasper preformance engine. I've seen no adverse effects by using NOS, Just good effects  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. If you follow the instructions that come with the kit to the letter you shouldn't have any problems. I did replace my stock fuel pump with a higher flowing pump.<P>I placed my bottle in the bottom right hand side of the trunk, I didn't and don't plan on hiding my bottle. (As far as I know it's not illegal to have Nitrous installed in any state). <P>Check out these links, Some of our fourm members sites. <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178/Page2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178/Page2.html</A>  <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/hyptnotise" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/hyptnotise</A> <P>here's a good Nos info page  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/5753/nitrous.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/5753/nitrous.html</A> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>-Brian S. <BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered and On The Bottle||||reg||10
Z||000002||fropuff||11-08-2000||09:46 PM||||That's good that it's not illegal; I thought it was.  That gave me some good information.  I'm not worried too much about premature wear; I won't use it much.  I was thinking of a 70 shot as well.  Now, I am looking for some results.  Like, I was wondering what a 70 shot of NOS on a bone stock engine will do.  None of the mods or anything like that.  Bone stock.  Can I find some results anywhere?  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||11-08-2000||11:52 PM||||use the search function and look for previous posts about nitrous oxide.  You will find lots of info as there is a new thread about nitrous every few days or so.<P>Also check the links that were given to you by sluppy.  That will give you some performance numbers as to what Fieros with nitrous can do.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
