Z||000005||fropuff||11-09-2000||08:35 PM||||Okay, I think I'll be getting nitrous.  I weighed all the possibilities, and I think there's more positive than negative.  I would not use it much at all anyway, so it couldn't do too much.  If I hook it up correctly and follow all directions, I should be fine.  Those results of 1FST2M6s are incredible!  He said he got a 4.9 0-60 time.  That's really good!  That's with a minimal amount of modifications.  That's what I'm basically worried about.  I don't really care about the top end, as I wouldn't get much of a chance to reach it.  Of course, I've got an auto, so it won't be as good as his, but it will cut it by around 2 seconds.  I don't really know what to do about a bottle, however.  I don't know if I should stand it up in the rear, or put in the front trunk.  I went on a site, and it said to have it angled at 15*, nozzle higher than the bottom.  It said to have the label and nozzle out as well.  I'm not sure yet.  I don't think I would get it from Fiero Store; NOS maybe.  $499 isn't bad at all.  Thanks for all the help.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000006||zeusrekning||11-09-2000||09:34 PM||||I noticed on hyptnotise's web page it says<BR>"Splayed Main Caps on #'s 2&3," What is Splayed? I've heard this term used but???<BR>And why only 2&3||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shaun41178||11-10-2000||01:21 AM||||Splayed means that the bolts do not go in perpendicular to to the block.  Normal bolts go into the block through the main caps at a 90* angle.  Splayed go into the block atg about a 45* angle or so.  Basically what this does is add 2 bolts to each intermediate main cap and hence making them stronger because as the cap would want to loosen under high stress the splayed bolts because of the angle they are at and since they are angled towards each other prevent the main cap from loosening.  Basically what they do is reinforce the block and main caps from destructing under high stress.<P>They are only on the middle two because the rear one is for the seal and the front one uses the timing chain cover.  Plus there is not enough material in those places either to add 4 bolt caps.<P>I have a pic of what I am talking about if anyone here would like to see it. <P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
